From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:31:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] audio: support a legacy HAL built with the Nougat audio.h

Android 9 inserted get_microphones() in front of dump() in audio_hw_device,
so for a HAL built against the Android 7 header each field from there on
holds the function of the next one: get_master_mute() runs the HAL's
create_audio_patch(), create_audio_patch() its release_audio_patch(), and
so on. Its audio_stream_out/in end at get_presentation_position() /
get_capture_position(), so the MMAP fields and all later ones are read past
the end of the HAL's structures.

ro.vendor.audio.legacy_nougat_abi marks the primary module as such a HAL
(Device::hasNougatAbi()). Methods that would read these fields report
NOT_SUPPORTED or do nothing, the device dump is skipped, and audio patches
are reported unsupported, so AudioFlinger routes with
set_parameters("routing=..."). The other modules keep the full interface.

Seen on the Meizu MX6 with audio.primary.mt6797.so from Flyme 8.0.5.0A
(Android 7.1.1, API 3.0): setEventCallback() jumped to string bytes, and
AudioFlinger's startup getMasterMute() ran the blob's createAudioPatch()
with garbage arguments.

Change-Id: Id1cf438b7fe40fea5aa921e5f2f1e48b444cb75c

